-- חוק הגנת השכר, התשי"ח-1958 — sections 1 and 9: when a month's wage
-- falls due and when it counts as withheld; section 19א: when what an
-- employer owes a provident fund counts as wages withheld, and the
-- compensation on it; section 20: when severance pay falls due, when it is
-- late, and the compensation for its lateness; and section 25: what may be
-- deducted from wages, and how much. The text is
-- laws/wage-protection-law.toml, pinned from the live page of ספר החוקים
-- הפתוח; the corpus holds no copy (MMS-601).
--
-- Why it is here: each sets a floor an instrument cannot go below. An
-- agreement or a circular that deems an overpayment "an advance on wages
-- for §25(א)(7)" and deducts it in twelve parts deducts only what §25
-- permits; the takanon's §1.28.2.3 restates §20 for teaching employees,
-- so where its restatement gives the employee less, the law governs (the
-- root's precedence, l4/lib/precedence.l4); and the provident-fund
-- agreements of 17.12.1998 apply the law to the monthly contribution,
-- which §19א makes wages withheld when it is paid late.
--
-- Days are counted as numbers here, as the takanon's restatement counts
-- them: a day is a serial, and a span of days their difference.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT vocabulary

§ `חוק הגנת השכר — מועד השכר, חוב לקופת גמל, פיצויי פיטורים שהולנו, וניכויים מהשכר`

§§ `1`

-- Of the definitions, those the sections here read. "שכר עבודה" includes
-- holiday pay, productivity and overtime pay and the other payments due to
-- the employee for his work and during it. "שכר מולן" is wages not paid by
-- the determining day. A "קופת גמל" is, among the rest, a pension or
-- provident fund the employer (with the employee, or alone) must pay under
-- a collective agreement or an extension order. "היום הקובע" is the ninth
-- day after the day the wage falls due under §§9, 10, 11, 13, 14 and 16(ב)
-- (the twenty-first, for one in national service in agriculture under the
-- Penal Law, whom no instrument of the corpus employs). "הפרשי הצמדה" are
-- the consumer price index's differences over the period, an input.
@ref law:1
`the days after the due day to the determining day, under section 1` MEANS 9

GIVEN `the day the wage falls due` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the determining day under section 1` `the day the wage falls due` IS
    `the day the wage falls due` PLUS `the days after the due day to the determining day, under section 1`

GIVEN `the day the wage falls due` IS A NUMBER, `the day it is paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the wage is withheld under section 1` `the day the wage falls due` `the day it is paid` IF
    `the day it is paid` GREATER THAN `the determining day under section 1` `the day the wage falls due`

GIVEN `the employer must pay it under a collective agreement or an extension order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee is a member of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a provident fund under section 1` `the employer must pay it under a collective agreement or an extension order` `the employee is a member of it` IF
        `the employer must pay it under a collective agreement or an extension order`
    OR `the employee is a member of it`

#ASSERT `the determining day under section 1` 31 EQUALS 40
#ASSERT NOT `the wage is withheld under section 1` 31 40
#ASSERT `the wage is withheld under section 1` 31 41

§§ `9`

-- A wage paid by the month falls due with the end of the month it is paid
-- for; one paid by a longer period is, month by month, its proportional
-- part, as if paid by the month.
@ref law:9
GIVEN `the last day of the month it is paid for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the day a monthly wage falls due under section 9` `the last day of the month it is paid for` IS
    `the last day of the month it is paid for`

GIVEN `the wage for the period` IS A NUMBER, `the months of the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the part of a longer period's wage due each month under section 9` `the wage for the period` `the months of the period` IS
    `the wage for the period` DIVIDED BY `the months of the period`

#ASSERT `the part of a longer period's wage due each month under section 9` 1200 12 EQUALS 100

§§ `19א`

-- (א): what the employer owes a provident fund counts as wages withheld —
-- whether he owes it directly or must deduct it from the employee's wage —
-- if it is not paid to the fund within 21 days of the day the wage it is
-- owed on counts (or would count) as withheld; whether or not that wage
-- was itself withheld. (ב): the compensation is, (1) on what he had to
-- deduct, §17's (not pinned), and (2) on what he owes directly, "the
-- debt": the linkage differences from the day the wage falls due to the
-- day the debt is paid, and 20% of the debt and the differences together
-- for every month it went unpaid, a part of a month pro rata. The rest of
-- the section (the fund's own duties toward the employee) is not pinned.
@ref law:19א
`the days section 19א(א) gives to pay the fund` MEANS 21

`why section 19א(ב)(1) gives no amount here` MEANS
    `not yet encoded` "סעיף 17 לחוק הגנת השכר (פיצוי הלנת שכר), שסעיף 19א(ב)(1) מפנה אליו"

GIVEN `the day the wage it is owed on falls due` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the last day to pay the fund under section 19א` `the day the wage it is owed on falls due` IS
    `the determining day under section 1` `the day the wage it is owed on falls due`
        PLUS `the days section 19א(א) gives to pay the fund`

GIVEN `the day the wage it is owed on falls due` IS A NUMBER, `the day the fund is paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the debt to the fund counts as wages withheld under section 19א` `the day the wage it is owed on falls due` `the day the fund is paid` IF
    `the day the fund is paid` GREATER THAN `the last day to pay the fund under section 19א` `the day the wage it is owed on falls due`

GIVEN `the debt` IS A NUMBER
      `the linkage differences` IS A NUMBER @desc by the consumer price index, from the day the wage falls due to the day the debt is paid
      `the months it went unpaid` IS A NUMBER @desc a part of a month as a fraction
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the compensation on a debt to the fund under section 19א(ב)(2)` `the debt` `the linkage differences` `the months it went unpaid` IS
    `the linkage differences` PLUS (`the debt` PLUS `the linkage differences`) TIMES 20% TIMES `the months it went unpaid`

-- An instrument that sets a day of its own for a contribution falls below
-- §19א only if that day is later than the last day the section lets the
-- debt go unpaid before it counts as wages withheld; an earlier day adds
-- to the law.
GIVEN `the day the instrument has the contribution paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the wage it is owed on falls due` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument's day for a contribution is later than section 19א allows` `the day the instrument has the contribution paid` `the day the wage it is owed on falls due` IF
    `the day the instrument has the contribution paid` GREATER THAN `the last day to pay the fund under section 19א` `the day the wage it is owed on falls due`

#ASSERT `the last day to pay the fund under section 19א` 31 EQUALS 61
#ASSERT NOT `the debt to the fund counts as wages withheld under section 19א` 31 61
#ASSERT `the debt to the fund counts as wages withheld under section 19א` 31 62
#ASSERT `the compensation on a debt to the fund under section 19א(ב)(2)` 1000 10 0.5 EQUALS 111
#ASSERT NOT `the instrument's day for a contribution is later than section 19א allows` 31 31

§§ `20`

-- (א): the day severance pay falls due is the latest of (1) the day
-- employment ended, and the later days (2)–(5) set where they arise: the
-- day a collective agreement, arrangement or extension order sets; for a
-- right above the statutory one, the day its contract sets (or the day the
-- right was set, if after the end); a right set collectively after the end
-- with no day, the day it was set; a right conditional on something after
-- the end, the day the condition is met.
@ref law:20
GIVEN `the day employment ended` IS A NUMBER
      `the later days (2)–(5) set` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc each of (2)–(5) that arises; empty if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the day severance falls due under section 20(א)` `the day employment ended` `the later days (2)–(5) set` IS
    maximum (`the day employment ended` FOLLOWED BY `the later days (2)–(5) set`)

-- (ב): severance not paid within 15 days of the day it fell due is late.
-- Paid on days 16 to 30 after it: the linkage differences from that day
-- to the day of payment. Paid later: the linkage differences, and 20% of
-- the severance and the differences together for every month it went
-- unpaid, a part of a month pro rata. (ב1): the compensation is part of
-- the severance for every purpose but (ב). The linkage differences are the
-- consumer price index's (the law's §1), an input; the months unpaid are
-- an input, a part of a month as a fraction.
GIVEN `the severance` IS A NUMBER
      `days from the due day to payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the linkage differences` IS A NUMBER @desc by the consumer price index, from the due day to the day of payment
      `the months it went unpaid` IS A NUMBER @desc a part of a month as a fraction
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the compensation for late severance under section 20(ב)` `the severance` `days from the due day to payment` `the linkage differences` `the months it went unpaid` IS
    BRANCH IF `days from the due day to payment` AT MOST 15 THEN 0
           IF `days from the due day to payment` AT MOST 30 THEN `the linkage differences`
           OTHERWISE `the linkage differences` PLUS `the 20% for the months unpaid`
    WHERE
        `the 20% for the months unpaid` MEANS
            (`the severance` PLUS `the linkage differences`) TIMES 20% TIMES `the months it went unpaid`

-- (ב2): the employer may set off from the severance and the compensation a
-- debt the employee owes him, or a sum he must or may deduct from the
-- severance. (ג): one entitled other than under §§1(א) or 5 of the
-- Severance Pay Law has no due day until he has demanded payment in
-- writing, stating the ground; a later demand moves the due day to it.
GIVEN `entitled under section 1(א) or 5 of the Severance Pay Law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the due day under (א)` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of the written demand` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the due day after a written demand under section 20(ג)` `entitled under section 1(א) or 5 of the Severance Pay Law` `the due day under (א)` `the day of the written demand` IS
    IF `entitled under section 1(א) or 5 of the Severance Pay Law`
    THEN `the due day under (א)`
    ELSE max `the due day under (א)` `the day of the written demand`

-- (ד): §§17א, 18 and 19 apply to late severance as to late wages (they
-- are not pinned); a regional court may reduce or cancel the compensation
-- also where the severance was held back for a real dispute over the
-- right, a dispute over the day employment ended, or particulars the
-- claimant did not give.
DECLARE `why severance was held back, under section 20(ד)` IS ONE OF
    `a real dispute over the right to severance`
    `a dispute over the day employment ended`
    `particulars the claimant did not give the employer`
    `another cause of the delay`

GIVEN r IS A `why severance was held back, under section 20(ד)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 20(ד) lets the court reduce or cancel the compensation for` r IF
    NOT r EQUALS `another cause of the delay`

-- (ה): one entitled to severance from a provident fund, by the employer's
-- payments to it, has no compensation for lateness on what the fund owes
-- him if the employer told the fund in writing, within 15 days of the due
-- day, that it consents to the payment. (ו): a deceased's severance the
-- employer deposited with the regional court is paid, for (ב), on the day
-- of the deposit.
GIVEN `the employer told the fund in writing it consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days from the due day to that notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 20(ה) leaves no compensation on what the fund owes` `the employer told the fund in writing it consents` `days from the due day to that notice` IF
        `the employer told the fund in writing it consents`
    AND `days from the due day to that notice` AT MOST `the days section 20(ה) gives the employer to notify the fund`

`the days section 20(ה) gives the employer to notify the fund` MEANS 15

#ASSERT `the day severance falls due under section 20(א)` 100 (LIST 90, 130) EQUALS 130
#ASSERT `the day severance falls due under section 20(א)` 100 EMPTY EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the compensation for late severance under section 20(ב)` 50000 15 400 0.5 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the compensation for late severance under section 20(ב)` 50000 25 400 0.8 EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `the compensation for late severance under section 20(ב)` 50000 45 400 1.5 EQUALS 15520
#ASSERT `the due day after a written demand under section 20(ג)` FALSE 100 140 EQUALS 140
#ASSERT `section 20(ה) leaves no compensation on what the fund owes` TRUE 15
#ASSERT NOT `section 20(ה) leaves no compensation on what the fund owes` TRUE 16
#ASSERT `section 20(ד) lets the court reduce or cancel the compensation for` `a dispute over the day employment ended`

§§ `25`

-- (א): nothing is deducted from wages but these: (1) a sum an enactment
-- requires or permits to be deducted; (2) donations the employee agreed in
-- writing to have deducted; (3) dues to a workers' organisation he is a
-- member of, deducted under a collective agreement or contract or with his
-- written consent, and the regular payments to the works committee; (3א)
-- an addition to those dues for party activity, unless he objected in
-- writing; (3ב) an agency fee for the representative organisation, from a
-- non-member, under a collective agreement or contract or with his written
-- consent (its maximum is set by regulations); (4) a disciplinary fine
-- under a collective agreement or an enactment; (5) current payments to
-- provident funds — save that a fund only the employee must pay is not
-- deducted if he objected in writing; (6) a debt under the employee's
-- written undertaking to the employer, no more than a quarter of the wage
-- deducted for it; (7) advances on account of wages, up to three months'
-- wages — beyond that, (6) governs the rest.
@ref law:25
DECLARE `deduction under section 25 of the Wage Protection Law` IS ONE OF
    `a sum an enactment requires or permits to be deducted`
    `a donation the employee agreed in writing to have deducted`
    `union dues or works-committee payments as (3) allows`
    `a party-funding addition to the dues the employee did not object to`
    `an agency fee as (3ב) allows`
    `a disciplinary fine under a collective agreement or an enactment`
    `a current provident-fund payment (5) allows`
    `a debt under the employee's written undertaking`
    `an advance on account of wages`
    `a deduction section 25 does not list`

GIVEN k IS A `deduction under section 25 of the Wage Protection Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 25 of the Wage Protection Law permits the deduction` k IF
    NOT k EQUALS `a deduction section 25 does not list`

-- (6): no more than a quarter of the wage is deducted in a month for a debt.
GIVEN `the month's wage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the most section 25(א)(6) lets be deducted in a month` `the month's wage` IS
    `the month's wage` DIVIDED BY 4

-- (7): of advances, as much as three months' wages is deducted as an
-- advance, with no limit to the month; the rest is a debt under (6). In a
-- month, then, the employer may deduct what is left of the advance part,
-- and at most a quarter of the wage toward the rest. The advance part is
-- taken to be deducted first (convention amounts.advance-part-first, a
-- pick put to the lawyer: (7) does not say which part a deduction pays).
GIVEN `the advances` IS A NUMBER
      `the month's wage` IS A NUMBER
      `already deducted` IS A NUMBER @desc what has been deducted of the advances in earlier months
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the most section 25 lets be deducted of advances this month` `the advances` `the month's wage` `already deducted` IS
    `what is left of the advance part` PLUS `the quarter toward the rest`
    WHERE
        `the advance part` MEANS min `the advances` (3 TIMES `the month's wage`)
        `what is left of the advance part` MEANS max 0 (`the advance part` MINUS `already deducted`)
        `the quarter toward the rest` MEANS
            IF `the advances` GREATER THAN `the advance part`
            THEN `the most section 25(א)(6) lets be deducted in a month` `the month's wage`
            ELSE 0

-- An advance deducted in equal monthly parts — as the agreements and
-- circulars that deem an overpayment an advance under (7) deduct it —
-- stays within §25 in every month only if no part exceeds what §25 lets be
-- deducted that month.
GIVEN `the advances` IS A NUMBER
      `the month's wage` IS A NUMBER
      `the parts` IS A NUMBER @desc the number of equal monthly parts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `equal monthly parts of the advance stay within section 25` `the advances` `the month's wage` `the parts` IF
    all (GIVEN k YIELD
            `the advances` DIVIDED BY `the parts`
                AT MOST `the most section 25 lets be deducted of advances this month`
                            `the advances` `the month's wage` (k TIMES `the advances` DIVIDED BY `the parts`))
        (range 0 (`the parts` MINUS 1))

-- (ב): notwithstanding (א), when the employee stops working for the
-- employer, the employer may deduct from his last wage any balance of a
-- debt he owes, advances among it.
GIVEN `the employee has stopped working for the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the balance of his debt` IS A NUMBER
      `his last wage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what section 25(ב) lets be deducted from the last wage` `the employee has stopped working for the employer` `the balance of his debt` `his last wage` IS
    IF `the employee has stopped working for the employer`
    THEN min `the balance of his debt` `his last wage`
    ELSE 0

#ASSERT NOT `section 25 of the Wage Protection Law permits the deduction` `a deduction section 25 does not list`
#ASSERT `section 25 of the Wage Protection Law permits the deduction` `an advance on account of wages`
#ASSERT `the most section 25 lets be deducted of advances this month` 12000 10000 0 EQUALS 12000
#ASSERT `the most section 25 lets be deducted of advances this month` 36000 10000 30000 EQUALS 2500
#ASSERT `equal monthly parts of the advance stay within section 25` 30000 10000 12
#ASSERT NOT `equal monthly parts of the advance stay within section 25` 36000 10000 12
#ASSERT `what section 25(ב) lets be deducted from the last wage` TRUE 3000 8000 EQUALS 3000
